nodecode-frihet is a rewrite of Frihet-io's hermes-frihet:

  https://github.com/Frihet-io/hermes-frihet
  commit 72493236b16c5e1e2b6a5ada3674781a6da180a1
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Frihet-io (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the module that registered the plugin with the host
(frihet.py, __init__.py) is now one cell. /frihet status, setup, doctor and
operations, the unauthenticated initialize probe, the redaction of a key in a
failure's text, the read / draft-write / irreversible / unknown classifier and
the pre-call gate that escalates the last two are all here, in Common Lisp,
against Nodecode's cell contract instead of a Hermes PluginContext. The one
tool the plugin needed the host for (a call into an MCP operation) is made by
the cell itself: JSON-RPC over HTTPS -- initialize, notifications/
initialized, tools/list, tools/call -- with the same endpoint, the same
tri-state report and the same fail-closed default.

Left out: the vendor/frihet-mcp-onboarding.json table of operations with
external side effects, which the cell folds into the operation-name patterns
it already had as a fallback; the host's own MCP client (Hermes's OAuth
cache, breaker and reconnect), so a call here carries the section's API key
rather than a host session; the ~/.hermes/config.yaml check, which has no
subject in Nodecode (the config is read by the section declaration); and the
bundled skill file, whose operating contract is the (help :frihet) topic.
